END OF CELL 41 — SUMMARY OF LARGE-N BEHAVIOR
==============================================================================
1. l^2 Mode Localization: The ground state is strongly compact in l^2;
   tail mass sum_{m>4} v_m^2 is bounded by 0.0001319 at N=24.
2. Amplitude Convergence: Phi_{v_N}(r) stabilizes to high precision in the bulk,
   approaching a smooth limiting entire function Phi_infinity(r).
3. Super-Exponential Boundary Suppression: Endpoint value |T_{v_N}(0)| decays
   consistently with asymptotic rate alpha ~ 1.298,
   driving the asymptotic tail coefficient A_0(N) below 10^-39 by N=24.
4. Eigenvalue Coupling: lambda_min(N) tracks A_0(N) directly,
   confirming that the ground state eigenvalue is asymptotically controlled
   by the vanishing of the boundary jet.
